<spell-notebook "divider theming">
	<header level="1">
		Divider
		<header>A divider visually segments content into groups.</>
	</>
	<divider-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-divider-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a region, `:root`), or
			on the inner box through `::part(divider)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each
			through a private alias, so nothing inside blocks them.

			- A `section` divider swaps in `--ui-divider-section-margin`, whatever the base margin.
			- The text look is `--ui-divider-font-weight`, `-text-transform`, `-letter-spacing`, `-text-color`.
			- Never set the `--_ui-*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* every divider on the page */
			:root {
			  --ui-divider-line-color: var(--ui-border-color-strong);
			}
			/* one region */
			.sidebar {
			  --ui-divider-margin: 0.5em;
			}
			```
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-divider" playground>
				<p>Doggie treats are good for all times of the year. Proven to be eaten by 99.9% of all dogs worldwide.</>
				<ui-divider></>
				<p>Doggie treats are good for all times of the year. Proven to be eaten by 99.9% of all dogs worldwide.</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			Each theme of the set (Spell, Glass, Fruity, Merlot, Paper, Midnight, Crisp, Pop, Matrix) changes a divider's colours through the shared
			tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
